The CMS can now expose individual REST endpoints as MCP tools, including tools that take arguments. Endpoints are marked with the new @com.gentics.contentnode.rest.mcp.McpTool@ annotation, and their arguments with @com.gentics.contentnode.rest.mcp.McpToolParam@ (on a method parameter, or on a field of a @@BeanParam@ parameter bean); on startup they are found via a classpath scan and registered on the MCP server that is served at <code>/mcp</code>. As a first example, the @getActionLog@ endpoint of the admin resource ("/admin/actionlog") is now exposed as an MCP tool, with optional paging and filter arguments.
